{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You’re here for your fourth cycle of high-dose methotrexate for your CNS lymphoma. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m okay overall, but my right foot still burns a lot. It’s making it hard to walk even short distances."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see that’s been a persistent issue. We’ll keep working on managing that pain. Otherwise, no nausea, fever, or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that. My asthma’s been stable, and I haven’t had any headaches lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll start your methotrexate infusion today. We’ll give you IV fluids with sodium bicarbonate to protect your kidneys and help clear the drug faster."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need the leucovorin again afterward?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:07:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, starting 24 hours after the chemo. We’ll give it every six hours to reduce side effects. We’ll also check your methotrexate levels daily to guide the dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Last time my liver numbers went up again. Is that expected?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:09:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, transaminitis has happened with each cycle. It’s a known side effect. We’ll monitor it closely and adjust leucovorin if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my gabapentin? It’s not helping much with the foot pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:11:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We plan to increase it. You’re on 300 mg three times a day now. We’ll go up to 400 mg three times a day to see if that helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:12:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’d like to try that. And the oxycodone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-06-11 10:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can continue taking it as needed. We may increase the dose later if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-06-11 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The methotrexate infusion went smoothly. You tolerated it well. We’re continuing bicarbonate in your IV fluids to keep your urine alkaline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-06-11 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Any side effects so far?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-06-11 14:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "None serious. Your labs this morning showed mild anemia, but that’s expected. Liver enzymes are up—ALT was 84—so we’ll watch that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-06-12 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your first methotrexate level came back low, which is great. That means your body is clearing it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-06-12 09:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-06-12 09:32:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll keep monitoring. We’ve increased your leucovorin to 40 mg every six hours because your liver tests are worsening again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-06-12 09:33:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe with my ulcerative colitis? I stopped mesalamine, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-06-12 09:34:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we held mesalamine because it can interact with methotrexate. Your UC has been quiet, so we’re not worried for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-06-12 09:35:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my potassium was low yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-06-12 09:36:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re giving IV potassium. The bicarbonate can lower potassium, so we’re replacing it to keep your levels safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-06-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re scheduled to do a lumbar puncture today to check for any lymphoma cells in your spinal fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-06-13 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Didn’t we do one last time? Why again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-06-13 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did, but the lab misplaced part of the sample. They ran cytology, but not the cell count or flow. So we need to repeat it for full results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-06-13 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t know that. Is it safe to do another one so soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-06-13 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s safe. Most people tolerate it well. You might have a mild headache afterward, but we’ll have acetaminophen ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-06-13 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The lumbar puncture went well. We got a good sample and sent it for all the tests—cell count, flow cytometry, and cytology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-06-13 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any immediate findings?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-06-13 14:33:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, results will take a few days. But your opening pressure was normal, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest labs show your methotrexate is now undetectable. That’s excellent. You won’t need more leucovorin beyond today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. What about my liver?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still elevated, but we expected that. It should improve over the next week. We’ll follow up with outpatient labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my foot pain? I’m on the higher gabapentin now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve increased it to 400 mg three times a day. If it’s still not helping, we can discuss other options later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my dexamethasone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re tapering it down. You’ll take 3 mg every morning for five days, then 2 mg after that. This helps avoid withdrawal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And acyclovir for the cold sore?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-06-14 09:08:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue that until your steroid dose is very low. It helps prevent herpes outbreaks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Are all my results back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most are. Your methotrexate is cleared, liver tests are stable, and your LP sample was processed correctly this time. Results are pending and Dr. ___ will follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Gabapentin is now 400 mg three times a day. Oxycodone is increased to 10 mg every four hours as needed. Dexamethasone is 3 mg daily for five days, then 2 mg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And enoxaparin for my blood clots?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue 60 mg twice daily. You’re still at risk, so don’t stop it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When do I come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:08:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Two days earlier than last time for your next cycle. We’ll schedule it. Also, get your blood work done on ___ and fax the results to Dr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:09:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to do that. Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:10:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You’ve done really well this cycle. We’ll keep monitoring everything closely. Feel free to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:12:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge nurse will go over your instructions and prescriptions. You should be ready to leave in about an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:13:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’m looking forward to being home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:14:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll stay in touch. Take care, and we’ll see you soon for your next cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—your foot pain still doesn’t have a clear cause. MRI and ultrasound were normal. We’ll keep investigating at your follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:17:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know it’s frustrating, but I’m glad we’re not missing something serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. For now, we focus on symptom control and your lymphoma treatment. We’re on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes me feel better. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. That’s what we’re here for. Rest up, and we’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:22:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:25:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last question—should I watch for any warning signs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Call if you develop fever, severe nausea, confusion, worsening pain, or shortness of breath. Also, watch for mouth sores or rash."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:27:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2175-06-15 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re all set."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2175-06-11 09:28:00",
    "admission_end": "2175-06-15 11:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, multiple sclerosis, ulcerative colitis, and asthma was admitted for her fourth cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the infusion well, with no acute complications. Transaminitis recurred and was managed with increased leucovorin. A repeat lumbar puncture was performed due to a lost sample from a prior admission; results are pending. Her chronic right foot pain persisted without a clear cause, and gabapentin was increased to 400 mg three times daily. Oxycodone was also increased for better pain control, and dexamethasone was tapered. She remained stable throughout the admission, with no signs of infection or neurological decline, and was discharged home with outpatient follow-up for lab monitoring and pending CSF results.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Ulcerative colitis, unspecified",
      "Alkalosis",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Multiple sclerosis",
      "Anemia in neoplastic disease",
      "Antineoplastic chemotherapy induced anemia",
      "Pain in joint, ankle and foot",
      "Nonspecific elevation of levels of transaminase or lactic acid dehydrogenase [LDH]",
      "Herpes simplex without mention of complication",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Headache",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Antineoplastic and immunosuppressive drugs causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Long-term (current) use of other medications"
    ]
  }
}
